# nr-office-pdf-jpx-decode

JPEG 2000 decoding half of mixdog-pdf (tier-1, dequantisation, inverse DWT, component transforms, palette/cdef,
sYCC, 8-bit delivery). Nothing was compiled or run as Rust by the implementing agent (no cargo).

## 1. Module lines (lead-owned file)

File: native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/src/codec/jpx/mod.rs
Anchor: the module list, after the line `pub mod tiles;`. Add, in this order:

    pub mod dwt;
    pub mod mct;
    pub mod output;
    pub mod t1;

(The four files exist and need nothing else from mod.rs. `output::decode(&Image, Options)` is the entry point;
`DecodedImage::to_pixels(max_components)` delivers pdf.js's 8-bit interleaved bytes. The module doc comment of
mod.rs says tier-1 and the rest "follow in the decoding half": the lead may reword it to name the modules.)

## 2. Cargo

No dependency edge and no Cargo.toml change: every crate the new code and tests use (mixdog-office-base twin
helpers, mixdog-testkit, serde_json) is already a dependency of mixdog-pdf.

## 3. Fixture index (hot file)

File: native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json, array "sets", keep it sorted by "set" (after "office-journal*" /
before "office-ooxml*" as the sort puts it). Add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-jpx-pixels.mjs",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-jpx-pixels/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "8653520fe21f58d9a4ff49e81876cbd3aab9080bac6a5342e494919a4b2d24cb",
